PART E -- THE GATES, cheapest kill first
======================================================================================================================
E.1  LENSING VERSUS DYNAMICS -- THE DECISIVE CHECK.  Unlike the phonon, the polarisation charge -div(Pi) is a MASS
     density: it enters the 00 Einstein equation, so it bends light.  The question is whether it lenses IN PROPORTION
     to how it moves stars, i.e. whether its stress makes Phi != Psi.  Derive the stress, do not assume it.
      stress tensor: W/(rho_pol c^2) = 5.56325028026809e-18*g*r = (1/2) v^2/c^2  [v^2 = g r] -- the internal stress is v^2/c^2 of the phantom rest energy
      on the deep-MOND SPARC points: the anisotropic-stress slip |Phi-Psi|/Phi = O(v^2/c^2), median 4.04e-08, max 5.86e-07
      => M_dyn/M_lens = 1 + O(v^2/c^2) = 1.000000 on the median deep point (the phantom mass sources BOTH Phi and Psi equally)
      CONTRAST with the superfluid: there the anomaly was a FORCE with NO mass, so M_lens missed it entirely and the ratio was 5.6-6.5; here the anomaly IS mass, so the SAME v^2/c^2 is a CORRECTION to 1, not the whole signal.
  [PASS] E1a GATE 1 (i): the polarisation's own anisotropic stress is O(v^2/c^2) of its phantom rest-energy density (median ~1e-8), so the phantom mass sources Phi and Psi equally -- the SAME v^2/c^2 that made the superfluid FAIL is here a tiny correction to a ratio of 1   (|Phi-Psi|/Phi median 4.04e-08)
  [PASS] E1b GATE 1 (ii) -- THE DECISIVE PASS: dipolar dark matter predicts M_dyn/M_lens = 1.000 ~ 1 against the measured 1.02, because its MOND phantom is real gravitating mass (the polarisation charge) rather than a mass-less force -- it PASSES the gate that killed the superfluid   (predicted 1.000 vs measured 1.02/1.02; superfluid was 5.6-6.5)
      This is a GENUINE STRUCTURAL DIFFERENCE and it must be stated precisely: gravitational polarisation is the one emergent-MOND
      mechanism whose anomaly carries its own gravitating mass, so it does not fail L67's lensing gate.  The lane does NOT die here.

      On the KiDS mass bins the polarisation phantom's predicted lensing IS g_b*nu(g_b/a0) (the RAR itself), so it inherits the
      data's own universality: per-bin offset from the measured lensing RAR spans 0.033 dex (the model's nu is simple-mu-like,
      a fixed function of g_bar, so it is universal in shape like the data) -- the superfluid's 0.29-0.58 dex bin-to-bin failure does not occur.
  [PASS] E1c on the KiDS mass bins the dipolar phantom's lensing tracks the universal measured RAR (spread < 0.15 dex), because the phantom equals the RAR anomaly by construction -- again unlike the superfluid (0.29-0.58 dex low/spread)   (across-bin spread 0.033 dex)

E.2  SOLAR SYSTEM.  The model's interpolating function is simple-mu-like (mu -> 1 - 1/sqrt(x)), so the anomaly
     a_anom = sqrt(a0 g_b) falls only as a POWER at high acceleration -- the same slow return that stresses standard MOND.
      [canonical] bare (no-EFE) anomaly sqrt(a0 g_N) = 7.78e-08 m/s^2 -> phantom 1.8e+07x the Pitjev-Pitjeva bound; EFE-quenched residual ~ a0^2/g_N -> 1.6e-02x the bound
      [alt      ] bare (no-EFE) anomaly sqrt(a0 g_N) = 8.53e-08 m/s^2 -> phantom 2.0e+07x the Pitjev-Pitjeva bound; EFE-quenched residual ~ a0^2/g_N -> 2.3e-02x the bound
      the Solar System sits in the Galaxy's field a_ext = 1.29 a0; internally g_N(Saturn) = 6.5e-05 m/s^2 = 6.9e+05 a0 is deep-Newtonian,
      so the EFE quenches the bare anomaly to the residual quadrupole -- exactly standard MOND's Solar-System status: EFE + a sharp mu needed.
  [PASS] E2  GATE 2 MARGINAL/NOT PASSED cleanly: the model HAS a computable high-acceleration limit (mu -> 1), unlike the superfluid's EFT wall at Saturn, but its simple-mu transition leaves an EFE-quenched residual ~ a0^2/g_N at Saturn of order the Pitjev-Pitjeva bound -- standard MOND's own tension   (EFE-quenched residual 1.6e-02/2.3e-02x the Saturn bound (bare, no EFE: 2e+07x); a sharper mu would pass)
